# Cores this port builds that libretro-super's recipe does not carry.
#
# ⚠ THE RECIPE IS SOMEBODY ELSE'S FILE AND IT IS NOT ALWAYS RIGHT ABOUT THIS PORT.
# recipes/linux/cores-linux-x64-generic is fetched from libretro-super, so a core missing from it
# is simply never attempted here - not judged and rejected, never tried. That is how dosbox_pure
# went unbuilt for the whole life of this port while the three DOSBox cores that ARE in the recipe
# all fail: dosbox_core and dosbox_svn want SDL and do not link, and dosbox_svn_ce cannot even
# clone. dosbox_pure has its own backend, needs no SDL, and built here on the first attempt with
# no patches at all.
#
# The same file also goes stale: tic80's recipe line names a branch that no longer exists, and
# libretro/pcsx2 and libretro/duckstation have been DELETED from GitHub while still being listed.
#
# Format is the recipe's own, so a line can be moved either way without editing:
#   name  dir  url  branch  fetch  buildtype  makefile  subdir  [extra args]
#
# Appended to whatever --recipe points at, and a name here WINS over the same name in the recipe,
# so this file can also correct a stale line rather than only add a missing core.
dosbox_pure libretro-dosbox_pure https://github.com/schellingb/dosbox-pure.git main YES GENERIC Makefile .
# ⚠ CORRECTION, NOT AN ADDITION: the recipe says `master`, which upstream no longer has.
# git ls-remote https://github.com/nesbox/TIC-80.git lists clay, custom-menu, lovebyte,
# luajit, main - and no master. Nothing is wrong with the core; the recipe went stale.
tic80 libretro-tic80 https://github.com/nesbox/TIC-80.git main YES CMAKE Makefile builddir -DBUILD_PLAYER=OFF -DBUILD_SOKOL=OFF -DBUILD_SDL=OFF -DBUILD_DEMO_CARTS=OFF -DBUILD_LIBRETRO=ON
# ⚠ CORRECTION, NOT AN ADDITION, AND THE STALE FIELD IS THE SUBDIRECTORY. The recipe says the
# build directory is backends/platform/libretro/build; upstream has no such directory and has
# not for years - README.md there says `cd scummvm/backends/platform/libretro && make`. A
# subdirectory that does not exist makes build-cores.sh fall back to the clone root, where make
# meets ScummVM's OWN top-level Makefile and stops on
#     Makefile:122: *** You need to run ./configure before you can run make.
# which reads as a core needing an autotools step. It does not: the libretro backend's Makefile
# is self-contained. It fetches its own dependencies (libretro-deps, libretro-common) into
# backends/platform/libretro/deps and runs scripts/configure_engines.sh itself, both from
# $(shell ...) at parse time, so `make` alone is the whole build and GENERIC is the right type.
scummvm libretro-scummvm https://github.com/libretro/scummvm.git master YES GENERIC Makefile backends/platform/libretro
